Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:13:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix: retarget NativeWindowRelay when a WebContents changes
 owner window (#55955)

* fix: retarget NativeWindowRelay when a WebContents changes owner window

NativeWindowRelay::CreateForWebContents() kept the first window it was
given, so after a WebContentsView moved from one window to another its
relay still pointed at the old window. Readers of the relay then used the
wrong window: a <webview> guest attached afterwards took the old window
as its owner (or none once that window was closed), and the download save
dialog and macOS passkey sheet parented to it. Point an existing relay at
the new window instead, so it follows SetOwnerWindow().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NayLZmD3uy6pz3eYZRPE4t

* fix: propagate owner window changes to attached webviews and DevTools

A <webview> guest and the built-in DevTools frontend take their owner
window from their embedder or inspected WebContents only once, when the
guest attaches or DevTools open. After a WebContentsView moved to another
window, guests already attached in it and DevTools already open on it kept
the old window (or none once it was closed), so
BrowserWindow.fromWebContents() and the relay's readers used the wrong
window. Have SetOwnerWindow() pass the new owner on to attached guests and
to the built-in DevTools frontend. A custom frontend set with
setDevToolsWebContents() is app-owned and may live in its own window, so
it keeps its owner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NayLZmD3uy6pz3eYZRPE4t

* refactor: retarget the relay from SetOwnerWindow

NativeWindowRelay::CreateForWebContents goes back to creating the relay
only when there is none. SetOwnerWindow, its only caller, now points an
existing relay at the new window through a new SetNativeWindow setter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
